  "help": {
    "format": "restructuredtext",
    "content": "\n\n========\nSynopsis\n========\n\nSplits a paired dataset into two individual datasets (forward and reverse).\n\n===========\nDescription\n===========\n\nThis tool takes a single ``paired`` collection and extracts its two components — the **forward** and the **reverse** dataset — as separate output datasets.\n\nThis is the inverse of **Zip collections**, which combines two datasets into a pair.\n\n========\nExamples\n========\n\n**Unzip a paired collection**\n\nInput ``paired`` collection::\n\n Paired: \"Sample 1\"\n\n   forward  →  reads_R1.fastq\n   reverse  →  reads_R2.fastq\n\nOutputs::\n\n Forward dataset:  reads_R1.fastq\n Reverse dataset:  reads_R2.fastq\n\n-------\n\n.. image:: ${static_path}/images/tools/collection_ops/unzip.svg\n  :alt: Unzip a paired collection into forward and reverse datasets\n  :width: 500\n\n-------\n\n.. class:: infomark\n\nThis tool will create new history datasets copied from your input collections but your quota usage will not increase.\n\n  "
  }
}